      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THE FINAL DANCE (1) won at Geelong two runs ago but couldn't repeat the dose at his latest appearance over 1200m at this track, beaten 5.5 metres. Still, a sound effort and will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Meets a similar line up and he is capable of a return to the winner's list. ANGELS WATCHING (3) wturned in a better run last time out when second over 1720m at this track, beaten a neck. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Meets a similar line up and he can play a big role. HES CHARLIES ANGEL (4) must be considered after he finished third over 1690m at Shepparton two-and-a-half weeks ago. MONTANA PRIDE (9) is worth some thought after his last-start fourth over 1720m at this track on August 12.",
